        "original_id": "c62cfafe-2245-596a-b6c1-4d5e9c41eb4c",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: Sirkus Papukaija, Papukaija\n- Places: Finland, Finnish municipalities, tropical and subtropical regions\n- Concepts: parrots, psittacines, Psittaciformes, parrot clubs\n\nFacts:\n- Sirkus Papukaija, later simply called Papukaija, was a Finnish children's television show that ran from 1961 to 1968.\n- Sirkus Papukaija was broadcast every other Sunday.\n- Sirkus Papukaija involved numerous parrot clubs in various Finnish municipalities.\n- Parrots, also called psittacines, are birds in the order Psittaciformes.\n- The order Psittaciformes comprises roughly 393 species in 92 genera.\n- Parrots are found in most tropical and subtropical regions.",
